{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'da-g9-ideas', 'standard': 'DA:Cr1.1.Ia; DA:Cr1.1.Ib', 'assumes': 'da-g8-ideas', 'hands_on': 'da-g10-ideas', 'model_in': 'inspiration-list; movement-challenge; style-menu', 'model_out': 'inspiration-list; movement-challenge; style-menu', 'words': 'stimulus; strengths; demanding; original; analyze; test', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Try many sources of movement for one piece of choreography and analyze in the process log how each shaped it, then test dance elements to find the student's strengths and choose demanding moves for an original piece. What changes: analysis of how a stimulus shaped the piece. Assessed by a portfolio entry with a short analysis, scored on a short rubric. Level 1 bridge: the first unit teaches the grade 8 techniques and words Level 1 needs, as readiness, and claims no grade 8 id (at most 12 days in the full year, 6 on the 80-day short path, STANDARD.md 3.2)."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'da-g10-ideas', 'standard': 'DA:Cr1.1.IIa; DA:Cr1.1.IIb', 'assumes': 'da-g9-ideas', 'hands_on': 'da-g11-ideas', 'model_in': 'inspiration-list; movement-challenge; style-menu', 'model_out': 'inspiration-list; movement-challenge; style-menu', 'words': 'combine; invented; established; style; purposeful; compare', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Choreograph a dance that combines invented and established movement from gathered source material, blending the student's strengths with more than one style, and compare the approach with that of known choreographers. What changes: styles are blended and choreographers are compared. Assessed by a dance portfolio entry and a short comparison, scored on a short rubric. Teacher note: any dance of a community is studied from its own published teaching or a named practitioner first. A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it. Level 2 opens with a review unit of at most 6 days that serves as placement."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'da-g11-ideas', 'standard': 'DA:Cr1.1.IIIa; DA:Cr1.1.IIIb', 'assumes': 'da-g10-ideas', 'hands_on': 'da-g12-studio', 'model_in': 'inspiration-list; movement-challenge; style-menu', 'model_out': 'inspiration-list; movement-challenge; style-menu', 'words': 'voice; risk; intent; habit; surprising; stretch', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Make a dance that carries a stated intent from blended sources, taking risks to find a personal voice, then push past usual movement habits for surprising solutions and explain in the log how they strengthened the intent. What changes: risk and a personal voice, with the reasons stated. Assessed by a portfolio entry of a risk-taking piece and a defended explanation, scored on the Level 3 rubric. Level 3 opens with a review unit of at most 6 days that serves as placement.'}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'da-g9-form', 'standard': 'DA:Cr2.1.Ia; DA:Cr2.1.Ib', 'assumes': 'da-g8-form', 'hands_on': 'da-g10-form', 'model_in': 'start-middle-finish; choreographic-tools', 'model_out': 'start-middle-finish; choreographic-tools; artist-statement', 'words': "collaborate; structure; purpose; artist's statement; support; elements", 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Make a dance with others whose structure serves its purpose, and write an artist's statement on how structure and elements support it. What changes: a written artist's statement joins the making, where grade 8 only defined criteria. Assessed by a performed dance and its written statement, scored on a short rubric for structure, purpose and reasons."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'da-g10-form', 'standard': 'DA:Cr2.1.IIa; DA:Cr2.1.IIb', 'assumes': 'da-g9-form', 'hands_on': 'da-g11-form', 'model_in': 'start-middle-finish; choreographic-tools; artist-statement', 'model_out': 'start-middle-finish; choreographic-tools; artist-statement', 'words': 'original; design; composition; aesthetic; statement; analyze', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Make original dances alone and with others, analyze how their structure serves their purpose, and write a statement of the student's aesthetic to guide later choices. What changes: a personal aesthetic is stated and composition is analyzed, where level 1 wrote about one dance's purpose. Assessed by a portfolio entry of a dance with an aesthetic statement, scored on a short rubric."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'da-g11-form', 'standard': 'DA:Cr2.1.IIIa; DA:Cr2.1.IIIb', 'assumes': 'da-g10-form', 'hands_on': 'da-g12-studio', 'model_in': 'start-middle-finish; choreographic-tools; artist-statement', 'model_out': 'start-middle-finish; choreographic-tools; artist-statement', 'words': 'fluency; personal voice; heighten; viewpoint; cultural; justify', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Choreograph original dances with a personal voice, justify the choices that sharpen the purpose, and write a statement of the student's own cultural and artistic viewpoint. What changes: fluent original work and a viewpoint stated. Assessed by a portfolio of original dances and a defended statement, scored on the Level 3 rubric. Teacher note: a student names only a heritage they choose to name; no one is asked to represent a group."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'da-g9-revise', 'standard': 'DA:Cr3.1.Ia; DA:Cr3.1.Ib', 'assumes': 'da-g8-revise', 'hands_on': 'da-g10-revise', 'model_in': 'try-a-change; feedback-loop; change-log; dance-notation', 'model_out': 'try-a-change; feedback-loop; change-log; dance-notation', 'words': 'devices; structure; evaluate; compare; notation; section', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Rework a dance's devices and structure to make its purpose clearer and judge what the changes did, and compare two established notation methods by recording one section in each. What changes: devices and structure are reworked, and notation methods are compared, where grade 8 tried one method on an excerpt. Assessed by a revised dance with an evaluation and a notated section, scored on a short rubric."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'da-g10-revise', 'standard': 'DA:Cr3.1.IIa; DA:Cr3.1.IIb', 'assumes': 'da-g9-revise', 'hands_on': 'da-g11-revise', 'model_in': 'try-a-change; feedback-loop; change-log; dance-notation', 'model_out': 'try-a-change; feedback-loop; change-log; dance-notation', 'words': 'refine; criteria; feedback; strategy; media; plan', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Refine a dance's devices and structure against criteria and feedback and judge the student's own revisions, and plan how to record the whole dance with notation or media. What changes: a recording plan covers a whole dance, where level 1 notated a section. Assessed by a refined dance and a recording plan, scored on a short rubric."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'da-g11-revise', 'standard': 'DA:Cr3.1.IIIa; DA:Cr3.1.IIIb', 'assumes': 'da-g10-revise', 'hands_on': 'da-g12-studio', 'model_in': 'try-a-change; feedback-loop; change-log; dance-notation', 'model_out': 'try-a-change; feedback-loop; change-log; dance-notation', 'words': 'document; justify; reflection; complete; notation; record', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Refine devices, structure and criteria through reflection and feedback, log and defend each revision, and record a complete dance with an established notation method. What changes: a whole dance is notated and every revision is defended, where level 2 only planned the recording. Assessed by a portfolio entry of the revision record and the notated dance, scored on the Level 3 rubric.'}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'da-g9-elements', 'standard': 'DA:Pr4.1.Ia; DA:Pr4.1.Ib; DA:Pr4.1.Ic', 'assumes': 'da-g8-elements', 'hands_on': 'da-g10-elements', 'model_in': 'dance-elements; energy-words; accent-and-timing', 'model_out': 'dance-elements; energy-words; accent-and-timing', 'words': 'partner; balance; contrast; syncopation; accent; whole body', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Build partner and group sections with low balances at contrasting levels, use syncopation and accents at varied tempos, take cues from the accompaniment, and carry energy through the whole body. What changes: partner balances and syncopation arrive, with a solo version of every balance always offered. Assessed by a performed phrase scored on a short rubric. Teacher note: no lifts; partner contact only by agreement and never required; balances are low to the floor, by agreement, with a solo version always offered.'}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'da-g10-elements', 'standard': 'DA:Pr4.1.IIa; DA:Pr4.1.IIb; DA:Pr4.1.IIc', 'assumes': 'da-g9-elements', 'hands_on': 'da-g11-elements', 'model_in': 'dance-elements; energy-words; accent-and-timing', 'model_out': 'dance-elements; energy-words; accent-and-timing', 'words': 'complex; purposeful; unpredictable; inner rhythm; initiate; transition', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Dance alone or with others using space on purpose in ground and aerial sequences, use unpredictable timing with phrasing from an inner rhythm, and start each phrase with energy that flows into the next. What changes: space is used on purpose and timing is unpredictable, where level 1 built balances and syncopation. Assessed by a performed sequence scored on the Level 2 rubric. Teacher note: no lifts; partner contact only by agreement and never required; a solo version is always offered.'}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'da-g11-elements', 'standard': 'DA:Pr4.1.IIIa; DA:Pr4.1.IIIb; DA:Pr4.1.IIIc', 'assumes': 'da-g10-elements', 'hands_on': 'da-g12-perform', 'model_in': 'dance-elements; energy-words; accent-and-timing', 'model_out': 'dance-elements; energy-words; accent-and-timing', 'words': 'fullest range; audience; layered; phrasing; project; dynamics', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Use the fullest range of space with focus moving inward and outward toward an audience, layer several rhythms with or without music, and adjust dynamics over a broad range to carry an intent. What changes: the full spatial range is used toward an audience and rhythms are layered, where level 2 used space and timing on purpose. Assessed by a performed sequence scored on the Level 3 rubric. Teacher note: no lifts; partner contact only by agreement and never required; a solo version is always offered.'}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'da-g9-technique', 'standard': 'DA:Pr5.1.Ia; DA:Pr5.1.Ib; DA:Pr5.1.Ic', 'assumes': 'da-g8-technique', 'hands_on': 'da-g10-technique', 'model_in': 'dance-warm-up; phrase-recall; rehearsal-goals', 'model_out': 'dance-warm-up; phrase-recall; rehearsal-goals; rehearsal-plan', 'words': 'retain; choreography; plan; habits; rehearsal; video', 'cross_subject': 'physical-education:g9-dance-design (learning and designing dance sequences); health:g9-phw-evaluate-habits (judging habits that prevent injury)', 'notes': 'Retain and perform choreography with technical skill, plan healthy habits for dance and daily life, with food through an invented dancer, and plan rehearsals with peers, using a recording to analyze and justify practice choices. What changes: rehearsals are planned and analyzed from a recording, where grade 8 kept a personal progress record. Assessed by a rehearsal plan, a performed piece and an analysis, scored on a short rubric. Physical education designs and performs sequences too. Teacher note: no lifts; partner contact only by agreement and never required; a solo version is always offered. No student is recorded, photographed or filmed without the family\'s yes; a face or voice is never required (hands, the work or the sound alone will do); a student who does not want to be recorded is observed live and the teacher\'s mark stands; kept work stays on the student\'s, family\'s or school\'s own device. Teacher note: no task asks about a student\'s own diet, weight or body; food choices and eating plans are studied through an invented dancer or dancers in general (APPROACH.md, "Sensitive ground").'}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'da-g10-technique', 'standard': 'DA:Pr5.1.IIa; DA:Pr5.1.IIb; DA:Pr5.1.IIc', 'assumes': 'da-g9-technique', 'hands_on': 'da-g11-technique', 'model_in': 'dance-warm-up; phrase-recall; rehearsal-goals; rehearsal-plan', 'model_out': 'dance-warm-up; phrase-recall; rehearsal-goals; rehearsal-plan', 'words': 'demanding; goals; anatomy; eating plan; solo; reflect', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Perform demanding sequences with others to meet set goals in space, rhythm and dynamics, apply anatomy and healthy habits to technique, including an eating plan for an invented dancer, and plan and reflect on solo and group rehearsals. What changes: demanding sequences are met and solo and group rehearsals are planned, where level 1 planned one rehearsal. Assessed by a performed sequence and a rehearsal reflection, scored on the Level 2 rubric. Teacher note: no lifts; partner contact only by agreement and never required; a solo version is always offered. Teacher note: no task asks about a student\'s own diet, weight or body; food choices and eating plans are studied through an invented dancer or dancers in general (APPROACH.md, "Sensitive ground").'}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'da-g11-technique', 'standard': 'DA:Pr5.1.IIIa; DA:Pr5.1.IIIb; DA:Pr5.1.IIIc', 'assumes': 'da-g10-technique', 'hands_on': 'da-g12-perform', 'model_in': 'dance-warm-up; phrase-recall; rehearsal-goals; rehearsal-plan', 'model_out': 'dance-warm-up; phrase-recall; rehearsal-goals; rehearsal-plan', 'words': 'body-mind; complex; self-evaluate; research; lead; rehearsal', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Apply body-mind principles in complex solo, partner or group work and assess the student\'s own technique, research safe dancer practices and change one of the student\'s own, and lead rehearsals that attend to detail and expression. What changes: rehearsals are led by the student and safe practice is researched, where level 2 planned rehearsals. Assessed by a led rehearsal, a performed piece and a research note, scored on the Level 3 rubric. Teacher note: no lifts; partner contact only by agreement and never required; a solo version is always offered. Teacher note: no task asks about a student\'s own diet, weight or body; food choices and eating plans are studied through an invented dancer or dancers in general (APPROACH.md, "Sensitive ground").'}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'da-g9-stage', 'standard': 'DA:Pr6.1.Ia; DA:Pr6.1.Ib', 'assumes': 'da-g8-stage', 'hands_on': 'da-g10-stage', 'model_in': 'performing-space; stage-terms; performance-etiquette', 'model_out': 'performing-space; stage-terms; performance-etiquette; production-plan', 'words': 'leadership; documented; evaluate; production design; strengthen; options', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Lead with etiquette, apply notes, evaluate documented rehearsal methods with proper terms, and judge production design options and carry out the ones that serve the dance's purpose. What changes: rehearsal methods and design options are evaluated, where grade 8 led and designed. Assessed by a performed dance, a rehearsal evaluation and a design choice, scored on a short rubric."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'da-g10-stage', 'standard': 'DA:Pr6.1.IIa; DA:Pr6.1.IIb', 'assumes': 'da-g9-stage', 'hands_on': 'da-g11-stage', 'model_in': 'performing-space; stage-terms; performance-etiquette; production-plan', 'model_out': 'performing-space; stage-terms; performance-etiquette; production-plan', 'words': 'model; projection; concert; stage; plan; process', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Lead by example in rehearsal etiquette, strengthen projection, apply notes and judge the documented process, and work with a team to stage a concert in a theater or another space from a production plan. What changes: a whole concert is staged, where level 1 evaluated one dance's production. Assessed by the concert and a production plan, scored on the Level 2 rubric. Teacher note: a concert uses only dances that are original to the class, public domain or openly licensed."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'da-g11-stage', 'standard': 'DA:Pr6.1.IIIa; DA:Pr6.1.IIIb', 'assumes': 'da-g10-stage', 'hands_on': 'da-g12-perform', 'model_in': 'performing-space; stage-terms; performance-etiquette; production-plan', 'model_out': 'performing-space; stage-terms; performance-etiquette; production-plan', 'words': 'lead; portfolio; venues; organize; design; document', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Lead rehearsals, model etiquette, build projection strategies, keep a process portfolio, and stage concerts in more than one space, designing the production for each. What changes: more than one venue and a process portfolio, where level 2 staged one concert. Assessed by the concerts and a portfolio, scored on the Level 3 rubric.'}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'da-g9-respond', 'standard': 'DA:Re7.1.Ia; DA:Re7.1.Ib; DA:Re8.1.Ia; DA:Re9.1.Ia', 'assumes': 'da-g8-respond', 'hands_on': 'da-g10-respond', 'model_in': 'look-and-say; dance-look-describe-interpret; dance-reason-because; dance-criteria-card', 'model_out': 'look-and-say; dance-look-describe-interpret; dance-reason-because; dance-criteria-card', 'words': 'analyze; pattern; relationship; cultural context; compare; evaluation criteria', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Write an analysis of how repeated patterns serve a dance's purpose and how elements across styles and traditions carry intent in their cultural setting, then compare dances with criteria and dance terms. What changes: the analysis puts a dance in its cultural context, where grade 8 judged by content and style. Assessed by a written analysis scored on a short rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'da-g10-respond', 'standard': 'DA:Re7.1.IIa; DA:Re7.1.IIb; DA:Re8.1.IIa; DA:Re9.1.IIa', 'assumes': 'da-g9-respond', 'hands_on': 'da-g11-respond', 'model_in': 'look-and-say; dance-look-describe-interpret; dance-reason-because; dance-criteria-card', 'model_out': 'look-and-say; dance-look-describe-interpret; dance-reason-because; dance-criteria-card', 'words': 'form; meaning; compare; communication; setting; values', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Write an analysis of how repeated patterns build form and meaning, compare patterns across styles and how the differences shape what a dance says in its culture, and compare several dances with criteria, weighing the values of their societies. What changes: societal values are weighed in the comparison, where level 1 analyzed one dance in its cultural context. Assessed by a written critique scored on the Level 2 rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.'}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'da-g11-respond', 'standard': 'DA:Re7.1.IIIa; DA:Re7.1.IIIb; DA:Re8.1.IIIa; DA:Re9.1.IIIa', 'assumes': 'da-g10-respond', 'hands_on': 'da-g12-criticism', 'model_in': 'look-and-say; dance-look-describe-interpret; dance-reason-because; dance-criteria-card', 'model_out': 'look-and-say; dance-look-describe-interpret; dance-reason-because; dance-criteria-card', 'words': 'genre; structured; beauty; belief; taste; defend', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Write a critique set on dances in varied genres: how repeated patterns build sound choreography, how dance carries ideals of beauty and cultural beliefs, how elements and setting shape expression, and the student's own tastes, defended in a peer discussion. What changes: a personal taste is named and defended. Assessed by a written critique and a spoken defense, scored on the Level 3 rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'da-g9-connect', 'standard': 'DA:Cn10.1.Ia; DA:Cn10.1.Ib; DA:Cn11.1.Ia', 'assumes': 'da-g8-connect', 'hands_on': 'da-g10-connect', 'model_in': 'like-me-line; dance-two-ties; research-notes', 'model_out': 'like-me-line; dance-two-ties; research-notes', 'words': 'choreographer; evidence; research question; process; compare; periods', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Analyze with evidence a dance's ideas and how the choreographer's view shapes the student's reading, research a dance question with others and make a dance that answers it, and compare dances from chosen styles or periods with reasons they differ. What changes: a team's research question is answered in dance, where grade 8 researched two topics alone. Assessed by a performed answer and a written process comparison, scored on a short rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'da-g10-connect', 'standard': 'DA:Cn10.1.IIa; DA:Cn10.1.IIb; DA:Cn11.1.IIa', 'assumes': 'da-g9-connect', 'hands_on': 'da-g11-connect', 'model_in': 'like-me-line; dance-two-ties; research-notes', 'model_out': 'like-me-line; dance-two-ties; research-notes', 'words': 'linked; other subjects; context; insight; transfer; styles', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Research the setting of a dance that links to another subject, solve movement problems on a researched topic with others and discuss what carried over, and tie the technique and criteria of dances from many styles and eras to their people's views. What changes: what transferred between dance and another subject is discussed, where level 1 answered one question in dance. Assessed by a performed piece and a written insight, scored on the Level 2 rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'da-g11-connect', 'standard': 'DA:Cn10.1.IIIa; DA:Cn10.1.IIIb; DA:Cn11.1.IIIa', 'assumes': 'da-g10-connect', 'hands_on': 'da-g12-connect', 'model_in': 'like-me-line; dance-two-ties; research-notes', 'model_out': 'like-me-line; dance-two-ties; research-notes; career-capstone', 'words': 'review; grown; careers; capstone; interest; over time', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Put together a review of the student's own choreography across the years with notes on what changed, and complete a capstone on a dance career of interest, set beside dances from more than one era. What changes: the student's own work over time and a career capstone, where level 2 linked dance to other subjects. Assessed by a growth review and a capstone project, scored on the Level 3 rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'da', 'grade': '12', 'skill_id': 'da-g12-studio', 'standard': '~DA:Cr1.1.IIIa; ~DA:Cr2.1.IIIa; ~DA:Cr3.1.IIIa', 'assumes': 'da-g11-ideas; da-g11-form; da-g11-revise', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'inspiration-list; movement-challenge; style-menu; start-middle-finish; choreographic-tools; artist-statement; try-a-change; feedback-loop; change-log; dance-notation', 'model_out': 'inspiration-list; movement-challenge; style-menu; start-middle-finish; choreographic-tools; artist-statement; try-a-change; feedback-loop; change-log; dance-notation', 'words': 'self-directed; series; proposal; studio; revision; portfolio', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Level 4 is an optional year the student leads: a self-directed series of dances built from a written proposal, with ideas, form and revision repeated on new work. Assessed by a portfolio of the series and a defended artist's statement, scored on the same rubric as Level 3 with a higher bar for independence. The Level 3 ids are owned in grade 11; this year applies them to new, self-chosen choreography."}
