ound and an aerial passage with space used on purpose and safe landings; DA:Pr4.1.IIb, a look-for: an unpredictable timing choice and a spontaneous response to the teacher's cue. End-of-unit assessment (a showing day, then a kept-piece day): DA:Pr4.1.IIc, a look-for: phrases started with energy and linked without a stop; DA:Pr5.1.IIa, a look-for: the demanding group sequence meeting its set goals in space, rhythm and dynamics; DA:Pr5.1.IIb, a kept piece: an anatomy note on two moves and the invented dancer's eating plan, drafted, given written feedback and revised; DA:Pr5.1.IIc, a kept piece: the solo and group rehearsal plans and a reflection on what they achieved. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: the fullest spatial range toward an audience (Level 3). Tools: step cards for landings and floor work, an anatomy card, the rehearsal plan sheets, Curio Class's own. Free path: claps, a drum, the voice. Short path: 20 days | First owning unit of Level 2 because unit 8's blended styles and unit 10's concert need purposeful space and planned rehearsals; the same slot as unit 2, one level harder | Candidate: a work from Asia with ground work, described and linked | Hazards and controls: aerial work is jumps and leaps from the floor only, landings taught before any jump, no jumping from a raised surface; floor work on a clean floor, knees and elbows protected by technique (rolling on the side, never on the spine or the head); no inverted moves; no lifts. Food: the eating plan is for an invented dancer; no task asks about a student's own diet, weight or body; health's steps if a student tells something. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (moving unit). |
