7.1.IIb, a kept piece: a comparison of patterns in two of the four works and what the differences say in each culture; DA:Re9.1.IIa, a kept piece: a critique of three dances with criteria, weighing each society's values, drafted, given written feedback and revised; DA:Cr3.1.IIa, a look-for on the showing and the log: revisions made against named criteria and feedback, each evaluated; DA:Cr3.1.IIb, a kept piece: the recording plan for the whole dance. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: a complete dance notated (Level 3). Tools: work cards for each version, the criteria card, the notation sheets, Curio Class's own. Free path: pencil and sheets. Short path: 20 days | After unit 8 because the refinement reworks its dance; before unit 10 because the concert shows the refined dance and the research there needs this comparison habit | Candidate: a fourth dance from the Americas, described and linked | The Rite of Spring stages an invented sacrificial rite: it is a stage fiction, studied by watching and reading only, with no role play of the sacrifice (STANDARD.md 5 leave-out line). The 2021 cast: the sensitivity agent reads the École des Sables' and the foundation's own published words first. Dancing Grandmothers: the agent reads the company's own words first; a tie to a student's own grandparents is optional, with an invented or public option marked the same. Hazards and controls: as unit 7. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (moving unit). |
